    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Rayon is synthesized from wood pulp and is commonly referred to as artificial silk.",
        "Nylon was the first fully synthetic fibre, manufactured entirely from coal, water, and air without any natural raw materials.",
        "Polymers are large macromolecular structures formed by linking repeating chemical units called monomers through polymerisation.",
        "Thermoplastics deform and melt easily upon heating, allowing them to be remolded, whereas thermosetting plastics set permanently.",
        "Plastics are non-biodegradable, posing severe environmental hazards due to long-term persistence in soil and water bodies."
      ],
      "id": "cf9tqps"
    },
