    {
      "id": "oj4vorj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.FINAL HIGH-YIELD POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Rayon is derived from a natural source (wood pulp) but classified as a semi-synthetic fibre because of chemical processing.",
        "Bakelite and Melamine are classic thermosetting plastics; Bakelite is used for electrical switches while Melamine resists fire and is used for kitchenware.",
        "Teflon (Polytetrafluoroethylene) is frequently asked for its non-stick property due to high resistance to heat and oil.",
        "Resin Identification Codes range from 1 to 7, where PET is Code 1 and PVC is Code 3."
      ],
      "id": "n8vy9vy"
    },
